sanctioned: this program derives an Ipe.Db.Store from a record's typed columns and round-trips a row through Db.insertFields / Db.findWhere / Db.deleteWhere / Db.migrate over sqlite::memory:. Ipe.Db.Store is an Ipê-only addition with no counterpart in the reference backend, and Ipê emits Rust+sqlx while the reference emits a different backend, so a shared Main.ipe cannot run on both. Ipê's output is recorded as the correct reference. The three output lines assert, in order: (1) a full insert -> query-by-primary-key -> per-column decode round-trip returns a record equal to the original; (2) a value containing "'; DROP TABLE users; --" is bound as a positional parameter and stored + retrieved LITERALLY (parameterisation, not escaping — the table is not dropped and the query still succeeds); (3) a Store declared with a column identifier containing a quote/semicolon/space fails to build (fromColumns returns Err via validSqlIdent), so the injection never reaches SQL.
